Ether — third-party notices and what we do NOT redistribute
=================================================================

This application itself is MIT-licensed.

Tablet-side relay: `resources/android/arm64-v8a/udp2tcp`
--------------------------------------------------------
Our own program, built from `udp2tcp.c` in this repository with the Android NDK
(`aarch64-linux-android26-clang`).  Statically linked against nothing but
Bionic; it is pushed to `/data/local/tmp` at run time and removed by the app's
cleanup.  No Google code is included in it.

adb / platform-tools: downloaded, not shipped
---------------------------------------------
The app never bundles or installs adb.  If no usable adb is found on the machine
(`$ADB`, then `$PATH`, then the standard Android SDK locations — see
`src/main/platform.ts`), it downloads `platform-tools-latest-{linux,darwin,windows}.zip`
from `dl.google.com` into **its own data directory** and uses that copy for its
own child processes only.  That download is covered by the Android SDK Terms of
Service / the Android Software Development Kit License Agreement, which is why it
is kept out of this distribution and out of the system PATH.  Deleting the app's
data directory removes it completely.

Electron, TypeScript, electron-builder: build-time dependencies
--------------------------------------------------------------
Declared as `devDependencies` in `package.json`; Electron's own notices ship with
whatever package electron-builder produces.  There are no third-party runtime
dependencies: the ZIP reader (`src/main/zip.ts`), the relay, and the CLI are all
plain Node standard library.

